  "question": {
    "text": "A potential difference of <math><mn>220</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is applied across a rheostat of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>. The voltmeter <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> has a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> and distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math>&nbsp;is one-fourth of the distance from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> . The error in the reading of voltmeter is approximately -<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" height=\"142\" src=\"assets\\qt0031_9cc4110afc82.jpg\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" width=\"293\" />"
